.THS Sbatch 8L News.SH NAMESbatch - Collect and batch News article for remote system.SH SYNOPSIS.rawsbatch [-c|-c7|-cf|-cf7|-b|-s] [-B=<size>] [-t]       [-G=<grade>] [-f=<size>] [-C=<cmd>] [-n=<system>]       <system>.noraw.SH DESCRIPTION.ti +3Sbatch collects all article which should be send to a remote system.On default all articles are batched into one file until the size limitis reached. With.O -cyou can compress the news to get a better throughput..NO -cfforces `freeze' to be used instead of compresss..NO -c7will encode them after compression to transmit them over lines whichonly supports 7 Bit..NO -cf7will be used for 7 Bit channels with `freeze' to compress data..NO -sall articles are spooled as single files..NO -f=<size>gives the limit of a file in kBytes. the default is 50 kByte. .NO -B=<bitcount>To compress with another bitvalue than 16 (the default, use the optionto set the bitvalue to 12 to 16. .NO -G=<grade>If your delivering program accepts a grade character in the commandstring then you can change this here. .NO -C=<cmd>the delivery command can be changed with this to a complete new value. The command may contain two different sequences for inserting the gradecharacter and the system name.  These are.bold\%Sfor the system and.bold\%Gfor the grading..NO -tthis is for use with eight bit characters. If your neighbor host doesn'tsupport these characters then they are translated back to pure seven bitASCII. Currently only the german umlaute for ISO8859/1 are supported..NO -n=<system>If the name in the command to forward news differs from the filename thebatchfile is stored then this is used as the filename of the batchedarticles..EO.SH CAVEATSThe files are stored in temporary on /dd. If this too small things mayfail..SH BUGSMay be a lot, none known..SH FILES.O /h0/SPOOL/BATCHThe articles are stored herein, for each system one file with thefilename of the system. The format is an optional flagfield seperatedfrom the main filename by a bar.RB (` | ').Currently there are the two flags.RB ` N 'and.RB ` C 'for non-convert and convert from 8 bit (if these optiones are properinserted the `-t' option is obsolete.).EO.SH SEE ALSO Inews - in this distribution Rnews - in this distribution